<task id="043" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>A Document is a field-mapping source: the caller's Read on the document decides, through the Document access path (owner 2026-11-04)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService (follow-up)</phase>
    <gate>031 merged to master</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api (MappingSourceReadProbe, MappingSourceCallerMask, the push source check, the analysis create response); a caller Read decision (tags bff-api, security).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive caller Read decision on a new source table, shared by three paths, with the external-caller document narrowing; UAC-r2 reviews.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits AnalysisEndpoints.cs (031) and the mapping-source helpers that RecordCreationService calls; runs after 031 merges and does not overlap 044/045's files except through RecordCreationService's callers.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, field-mapping, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make sprk_document a usable field-mapping source. When the mapping source is a Document, the caller's Read on it is asked through the Document access path (FinanceAuthorizationFilter.DocumentEntitySet, the probe the document routes use), and a caller who is not an internal systemuser is also narrowed by InternalPlaneDocumentNarrowing. If the caller can read the document and may create (or, on push, update) the target, the document's mapped values are copied, fill-only, as for any other source. On the analysis create route, the mapping warnings are returned to the caller, not only logged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, field mapping and caller-context authorization. Security fails closed. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A Document to Analysis profile maps on analysis create (the 031 route), through the caller mask, and on push from a document, for a caller who can read the document; a caller who cannot, or an external caller the narrowing does not show the document to, gets no mapped values and the one uniform warning. EntityAccessFilter's map is unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner decision 2 of 2026-11-04 (notes/decisions.md, last section): "if the user can read the document and may create or update the analysis, the document's values map." Found in 031 (notes/task-031-notes.md, "Finding that needs an owner decision"). All three readers resolve the source's entity set through EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet, the association lockstep map, which holds no sprk_document entry, so a document source ends in MappingSourceRead.Unavailable today: MappingSourceReadProbe.CheckCallerReadAsync (~:150), MappingSourceCallerMask.ApplyAsync (~:120) and FieldMappingEndpoints.AuthorizePushSourceAsync (~:814). Line numbers are at master 0d4aa87ee0; re-grep.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/MappingSourceReadProbe.cs (CheckCallerReadAsync ~:142-174: a document branch before the TryResolveEntitySet miss)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/MappingSourceCallerMask.cs (ApplyAsync ~:120: the same entity-set answer for a document)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/FieldMappings/FieldMappingEndpoints.cs (AuthorizePushSourceAsync ~:808-830: the same document branch)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs (CreateAnalysis, as merged by 031: return outcome.Warnings in the 201 body)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/CreateAnalysisRequest.cs (CreateAnalysisResponse ~:25: an optional warnings member, omitted when empty)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/FieldMapping/MappingSourceReadProbeTests.cs and tests/integration/auth/FieldMapping/MappingSourceCallerMaskTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/seam/RecordCreation/RecordCreationServiceMappingSeamTests.TypedRoutes.cs (031's document-source test: flip it from "maps nothing" to "maps")</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs DocumentEntitySet (~:313) and AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.AttachDocumentCheck (~:781): the Document access path the analysis routes already ask</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/InternalPlaneDocumentNarrowing.cs (ForCallerAsync ~:57, NarrowForExternalCallerAsync ~:143, IsExternalOrUnknownCallerAsync ~:202): THE external document narrowing; reuse, never copy its rule</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs ~:305-307: how a route returns outcome.Warnings in its 201 body (omitted when empty)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/AssociationTypeLockstepTests.cs: must stay green unchanged</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="031" status="required">The analysis create route creates through RecordCreationService with a mapping request; its document-source test pins today's outcome.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-10-20">Brief line 1: `git switch -c task/fm-043 &lt;tip of work/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1&gt;` (must contain 031's merge), then confirm this POML exists on the branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-04">Scope of the change: a branch for sprk_document only, in the three readers named above. EntityAccessFilter's map (and so TryResolveEntitySet) is NOT changed: it is the association lockstep map that upload, record-route and Compose authorization share (AssociationTypeLockstepTests stays green with unchanged assertions).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-04 / NFR-01">Every non-allowed outcome for a document source (not readable as the caller, not shown by the narrowing, missing, a faulted probe or narrowing, no caller token) gives the same MappingSourceRead.Unavailable and the same SourceUnavailableWarning text; no refusal; the document is never read app-only before the caller's Read (and, for an external caller, the narrowing) has allowed it. The probe is GetCallerRightsForAuthorizationGateAsync under the existing "read" key, so a denied and an unknown id take the same work.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UAC-r2 task 188">A caller who is not a resolved internal systemuser maps from a document only when InternalPlaneDocumentNarrowing shows it; a narrowing fault shows none. The rule is reused through its existing methods, not re-implemented.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08">The create and push still need the caller's own permission on the target (Create on the analysis; Write on the pushed child, as push asks today). This task adds no new privilege question and no exemption.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">Every refusal on every route keeps its code, status and words. The analysis 201 body gains only an optional warnings member (absent when empty, the ChildRecordEndpoints shape); existing fields are unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">KEEP paths only (tests/integration/auth/**, tests/integration/seam/**, tests/integration/contract/**, tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/**); no new file under tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">No new DI registration or interface; the helpers stay static.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Placement and publish delta: see notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

