  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Branch (constraint 1); declare FULL rigor; /conflict-check for AnalysisEndpoints.cs, FieldMappingEndpoints.cs and the two FieldMapping helpers.</step>
    <step order="1">Write AC1-AC6 tests failing first (the 031 seam test flipped; probe and mask cases for a document source; push from a document).</step>
    <step order="2">Add ONE document entity-set answer shared by the three readers (FinanceAuthorizationFilter.DocumentEntitySet for sprk_document), used only where TryResolveEntitySet misses; every other table resolves exactly as today.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the external narrowing for a document source. Where the route already ran AttachDocumentCheck and the narrowing on the same document id (analysis create), reuse that decision rather than asking twice; elsewhere call the narrowing's existing method.</step>
    <step order="4">Return the create's warnings in the analysis 201 body.</step>
    <step order="5">Build; verify-suites.sh and ArchTests; publish delta; CVE.</step>
    <step order="6">Two adversarial passes (security tag), then the diff to UAC-r2 for its review. Fix every finding. Record in notes/task-043-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="7">After merge: TASK-INDEX `✅ [done]`; run scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a document source cannot be supported without adding sprk_document to EntityAccessFilter's map, or without a new DI registration, interface or service, STOP and escalate (owner + UAC-r2).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the narrowing cannot be reached from the service's mapping step without HttpContext and the route's decision cannot be passed in through the existing RecordCreationRequest shape, STOP and escalate with the options.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any existing refusal code, status or word, or any AssociationTypeLockstepTests assertion, would change, STOP and escalate (NFR-07).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">The five src files in relevant-files</output>
