  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1: analysis create through the 031 route with a Document to Analysis profile, the caller holding Read on the document: the profile's values are on the created analysis, fill-only (a value the request sends wins), and the warnings list is empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2 (negative): the same create where the caller cannot read the document, where the document does not exist, and where the probe faults: no mapped value, exactly one SourceUnavailableWarning, the analysis is still created (201) or refused exactly as today by the route filter; the three warnings are byte-identical, and the document is not read app-only (asserted by call order).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3 (negative): a caller who is not an internal systemuser, where the narrowing does not show the document, and where the narrowing faults: no mapped value and the same single warning. Where the narrowing shows it, AC1's outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4: MappingSourceCallerMask on a document source returns the caller-readable mapped columns (a field-secured one the caller cannot read is not copied), the same as for any other table.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5: push from a document source: a caller with Read on the document (and narrowed when external) pushes the Manual Refresh rules to the children the push already selects; a caller without Read gets push's existing uniform 404 with nothing read or written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6: the analysis 201 body carries the create's warnings (the RecordCreationWarning list) when there are any and no warnings member when there are none; every other field and every refusal of the route is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7 (must-not-fire): for every table in EntityAccessFilter's map, the three readers give the same decisions as before (existing suites green with unchanged assertions); AssociationTypeLockstepTests is unchanged and green; a table that is neither in the map nor sprk_document is still EntityTypeNotAuthorizable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC8: BFF build 0 errors, 0 warnings; verify-suites.sh and ArchTests (incl. MappingSourceCallerMaskGuardTests) pass; publish delta against a fresh master build and the CVE result are recorded; UAC-r2's verdict line is in the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: AC1-AC7 only; anything beyond needs a one-line reason in the notes. One seeding proof: remove the narrowing call once and show AC3 fails (recorded, reverted).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Placement Justification (CLAUDE.md §10, bff-extensions.md): a modification of three existing static readers and one existing route in the BFF, where the create-time mapping and the push already run; no new endpoint, service, registration, package or background work; expected publish delta ≈ 0, measured against a fresh master build; CVE check run.
§11: modify-only. The document branch reuses FinanceAuthorizationFilter.DocumentEntitySet and InternalPlaneDocumentNarrowing. If a shared helper method is added for the three readers, answer the three questions in the notes.
API contract: the analysis create response gains an optional warnings member (additive). The Analysis wizard's display of it belongs to task 028.
Release note: a Document to Analysis field-mapping profile now applies on analysis create and push for a user who can read the document.
Added 2026-11-04 from owner decision 2 (after the 031 review).</notes>

